{"repositoryId":958099590,"availability":"available","full":"tonioloewald/tosijs-3d","name":"tosijs-3d","description":"web-component that wraps babylonjs","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2025-03-31T16:36:13Z","updated":"2026-10-15T10:38:20Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://3d.tosijs.net/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:36.271Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:36.271Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:36.271Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T11:20:36.271Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["tosijs-3d is a library for building 3D web apps — and standalone apps, if that is what you want. Under the hood it uses Babylon.js for rendering, glTF/GLB for models and the usual bitmap formats for textures — but it also leans on SVG, for textures and for the entire user interface.","Free and open source, and light for what it is (Babylon is not small; this adds little to it). Scenes are composed from web components, so a world is markup you can read:","The doc site has about a hundred live demos you can edit in place; the b3d page is that scene running."],"features":["Procedural astronomical objects — planets, stars and star systems, galaxies, and black holes with accretion disk, photon ring and lensing. Generated, not modelled — a solar system is a few attributes.","Procedural terrain — streaming LOD terrain with a biome shader that runs one material from seafloor to mountain, a floating origin so worlds can be large, and carved landforms — volcanoes with lava tubes bored through…","Biped control — a character controller with an animation state machine and follow/XR cameras, from a GLB.","Aircraft control — a forgiving flight model that flies like a drone below transition speed and like a plane above it, with VTOL, bank-to-turn, a HUD and radar.","One UI for flat, in-scene and VR — the widget set renders as a DOM overlay, as a texture on a surface in the scene, and as a floating panel in a headset, from the same declaration. Includes a flowing box model, menus…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tonioloewald/tosijs-3d/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e5fd266c619325bd99a9844e5d1ce0f9e09578efdd31849c7c01f16d196c13cd","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:36.361Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:36.361Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"tosijs-3d is a library for building 3D web apps — and standalone apps, if that is what you want. Under the hood it uses Babylon.js for rendering, glTF/GLB for models and the usual bitmap formats for textures — but it also leans on SVG, for textures and for the entire user interface.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tonioloewald/tosijs-3d/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"e5fd266c619325bd99a9844e5d1ce0f9e09578efdd31849c7c01f16d196c13cd","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tonioloewald/tosijs-3d/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:36.362Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-15T10:38:20Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tonioloewald/tosijs-3d/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:36.362Z","hash":"e5fd266c619325bd99a9844e5d1ce0f9e09578efdd31849c7c01f16d196c13cd","originalBytes":8034,"storedBytes":8034,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["one","model","scene","world","b3d","bun","tosijs-3d","about","babylonjs","control","input","inside","keyboard","same","set","simulation","three","b3dskybox","b3dsun","because","controllers","doc","engine","every","flight","headset","install","live","surface","svg","terrain","textures","them","things","touch","what","widget","without","aircraft","already","app.","apps","attribute","b3dbox","b3dground","b3dsphere","babylon","bash","biome","both","capability","character","color","controlinput","deterministic","dev","device","documented","does","dom","drive","enter